# Vauxhall B-type 30 hp six landaulette, 1910-1914.
#
# Vauxhall used the letter B for two different cars: the B.09 16 hp four of
# 1908-1911 and the B.10, B.11 and B.12 sixes of 27, 30 and 35 hp built from
# 1909 to 1916. THIS OBJECT IS THE B.11 30 HP SIX, because that is the car the
# side photograph shows; the B.09 four is a different model and is NOT
# represented. The closed landaulette body is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_B-type
#
# Dimensions: wheelbase 3.429 m (135 in) or 3.658 m (144 in), width 1.626 m
# (64 in). No overall length or height is given, because they are
# body-dependent, so the length is measured from the photograph and the height
# is estimated.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a TRUE side elevation of car B11.39, parallel to
# the image plane with no yaw, camera near waist height. No front or rear
# photograph of any six-cylinder B-type exists in the pack, so the radiator
# face and lamp arrangement are inferred and recorded as inferred.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was found. Black, Dark Green,
# Maroon and Grey are period finishes. Weights 10, 9, 8, 7, total 34,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 110 km/h. Comfort 22/363, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 22. Classes 2,3.
# Dates: intro January 1910; retires staggered 1928-1932 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-b-type.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-b-type.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-b-type/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the length and height are estimated. The radiator face,
# the lamp arrangement, the rear finish and the opposite-side spare are
# inferred, no front or rear photograph of a six-cylinder B-type existing. The
# bonnet is closed in the model, whereas the museum car shows its engine.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallBType(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=10
intro_year=1910
intro_month=1
retire_year=1932
retire_month=6
speed=110
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=22
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=363

